|  This, then, is what has happened to a doctrine originally intended
|  only to protect the helpless. To make matters worse, the doctrine of
|  parens patriae has spilled out of courtrooms and into the ranks of family court auxiliaries - particularly the social workers and mental health
|  professionals who are called on to make judgments about the welfare
|  of families involved in litigation. One protective mother after another
.  has found a bureaucrat making the decisions for her children in matters that she has always believed (correctly) are secured to her by right


